<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>1.13.5: Practice</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m00293</md:content-id>
    <md:title>1.13.5: Practice</md:title>
    <md:uuid>30f02276-bfc9-450d-9129-4996b8e5cd32</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><para>Complete the following questions to practice the skills you have learned in this lesson.</para>
<div class="os-raise-ib-pset" data-button-text="Check" data-content-id="e4f07aa9-b95c-4c3a-b9e4-071b158d91f1" data-fire-learning-opportunity-event="eventnameY" data-fire-success-event="eventnameX" data-retry-limit="2" data-schema-version="1.0"><!--Q#1-->
  <exercise data-content-id="d746e47d-1480-40ae-a4c4-5f0f9911c402" data-problem-comparator="integer" data-problem-type="input" data-solution="5">
    <problem>
      <para> What is the slope of the line that goes through the points in the given table of values?</para>
      <table class="os-raise-horizontaltable">
        <thead>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <row>
            <entry scope="row" class="emphasis">\(x\)</entry>
            <entry>1</entry>
            <entry>2</entry>
            <entry>3</entry>
            <entry>4</entry>
          </row>
          <row>
            <entry scope="row" class="emphasis">\(y\)</entry>
            <entry>6</entry>
            <entry>11</entry>
            <entry>16</entry>
            <entry>21</entry>
          </row>
        </tbody>
      </table>
      
      <para>Enter your answer here.</para>
    </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! Since the change in \(y\) is 5, and the change in \(x\)is 1, the slope is \(\frac51\) or 5.</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activities 1.13.2 and 1.13.3.</para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--END QUESTION.-->
  <!--Q#2-->
  <exercise data-content-id="5b06c140-6d95-47bd-ae33-47e2866404fd" data-problem-comparator="integer" data-problem-type="input" data-solution="2">
    <problem>
      <para>In the equation, \(y = 4x + 2\), what is the value of the \(y\)-intercept?</para>
      <para>Enter your answer here.</para>
    </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! In the form, \(y=mx +b\), \(b\) is the \(y\)-intercept so 2 is the \(y\)-intercept in this equation.</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 1.13.1. </para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--Q#3-->
  <exercise data-content-id="f32865f8-862f-40d1-b4c1-fc95f906f760" data-problem-comparator="integer" data-problem-type="input" data-solution="3">
    <problem>
      <para>Identify the slope in the given graph.</para>
      <para><figure><media alt="Insert Alt Text"><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/46cec782dce063f1e452bb13a0ec3ba26a8cffdd"/></media></figure></para>
      <para>Enter your answer here.</para>
    </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! From the point \((-1,1)\) to \((0,4)\), the slope is 3.</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 1.13.3. </para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--Q#4-->
  <exercise data-content-id="67f9fa7e-8472-4e31-867a-fd8a46226ea4" data-problem-type="multiplechoice" data-retry-limit="3" data-solution="\(y=5x+2\)" data-solution-options="[&quot;\\(y=2x+5\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(y=5x+2\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(y=7x-2\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(y=5x-2\\)&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>Which of the following is an equation for the table of values?</para>
      <table class="os-raise-horizontaltable">
        <thead>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <row>
            <entry scope="row" class="emphasis">\(x\)</entry>
            <entry>0</entry>
            <entry>1</entry>
            <entry>2</entry>
            <entry>3</entry>
          </row>
          <row>
            <entry scope="row" class="emphasis">\(y\)</entry>
            <entry>2</entry>
            <entry>7</entry>
            <entry>12</entry>
            <entry>17</entry>
          </row>
        </tbody>
      </table>
      
    </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! The \(y\)-intercept is 2 and the slope is 5.</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activities 1.13.2 and 1.13.3.</para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--END QUESTION.-->
  <!--Q#5-->
  <exercise data-content-id="02f87ef5-ff24-4d92-8448-0da1ee9d0ea0" data-problem-comparator="float" data-problem-type="input" data-solution="-1">
    <problem>
      <para>For the equation \(y= -2x +3\), what is the value when \(x = 2\)?</para>
      <para>Enter your answer here.</para>
    </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! Substitute \(x=2\) so that \(y = -2(2)+3= -4+3=-1\).</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 1.13.4.</para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--Q#6-->
  <exercise data-content-id="096276e4-4e51-45b3-8b2b-014cfb1ee59f" data-problem-type="multiplechoice" data-retry-limit="3" data-solution="\(y=15w +40\)" data-solution-options="[&quot;\\(y=15w +40\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(y=40w\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(y=40w+15\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(y=40(15w)\\)&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>Jonah started the month with $40 and earned $15 each week walking dogs for neighbors. How much does he have after \(w\)  weeks?</para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! Jonah started with $40 so that is the \(y\)-intercept. He earned $15 each week so that is the slope.</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activities 1.13.2 and 1.13.3.</para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--END QUESTION.-->
  <!--Q#7-->
  <exercise data-content-id="d7acd21e-9f2a-4b1a-aa74-1130083fb59b" data-problem-comparator="integer" data-problem-type="input" data-solution="3">
    <problem>
      <para>Write the slope of the given table.</para>
      <table class="os-raise-horizontaltable">
        <thead>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <row>
            <entry scope="row" class="emphasis">\(x\)</entry>
            <entry>0</entry>
            <entry>2</entry>
            <entry>4</entry>
          </row>
          <row>
            <entry scope="row" class="emphasis">\(y\)</entry>
            <entry>5</entry>
            <entry>11</entry>
            <entry>17</entry>
          </row>
        </tbody>
      </table>
      
      <para>Enter your answer here.</para>
    </problem>
    <solution>
      <para> Correct! The change in \(y\) is 6 and the change in \(x\) is 2 so the slope is \(\frac62\) or 3.</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activities 1.13.2 and 1.13.3. </para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--Q#8-->
  <exercise data-content-id="6f2232f8-366d-46a3-bb45-08649f2af71b" data-problem-comparator="integer" data-problem-type="input" data-solution="5">
    <problem>
      <para>For the equation \(g=\frac{w+3}{2}\), what is the value of \(g\) when \(w=7\)?</para>
      <para>Enter your answer here.</para>
    </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! 5</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 1.13.4.</para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--Q#9-->
  <exercise data-content-id="2af60583-92e1-4fe3-a3e7-418324146104" data-problem-comparator="integer" data-problem-type="input" data-solution="1">
    <problem>
      <para>Identify the \(y\)-intercept of the given table.</para>
      <table class="os-raise-horizontaltable">
        <thead>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <row>
            <entry scope="row" class="emphasis">\(x\)</entry>
            <entry>1</entry>
            <entry>2</entry>
            <entry>3</entry>
          </row>
          <row>
            <entry scope="row" class="emphasis">\(y\)</entry>
            <entry>3</entry>
            <entry>5</entry>
            <entry>7</entry>
          </row>
        </tbody>
      </table>
      
      <para>Enter your answer here.</para>
    </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! Work backward using the pattern to when \(x =0\). Subtract 1 from \(x=1\) and subtract 2 from \(x=3\).</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 1.13.2. </para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--Q#10-->
  <exercise data-content-id="a0a731c8-f232-4ed5-8701-2a23e8395c7e" data-problem-comparator="text" data-problem-type="input" data-solution="-1/5">
    <problem>
      <para>Identify the slope of the line between \((3, 6)\) and \((-2, 7)\).</para>
      <para>Enter your answer here.</para>
    </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! \(- \frac15\)</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 1.13.1.</para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
